\section{Introduction}
South Fali (ISO 639-3 \texttt{fal}) is spoken in northern Cameroon by about 20,000 people; listed varieties include Kaang (Fali Kangou), Bele (Fali-Bele) and Fali-Tinguelin. The Peske variety belongs to North Fali, not South Fali. Search found no dictionary, primer or school programme.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia on the Fali languages of Cameroon: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fali_languages_(Cameroon)}
\item Joshua Project language page for \texttt{fal}: \url{https://www.joshuaproject.net/languages/fal}
\item Sweetman (1981), a comparative study of Fali dialects published by SIL Yaound\'e, is listed as further reading on the Wikipedia page; it was not itself located online.
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Joshua Project, South Fali in Cameroon: \url{https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/11183}
\item Scripture Earth page for \texttt{fal} (contents not inspected): \url{https://www.scriptureearth.org/00eng.php?iso=fal}
\end{itemize}

